<%- include("partials/header", { title, navLinks, activePath }) %>

<main class="container py-4">
  <section class="panel hero-panel">
    <div>
      <h2>Basic checklist</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Use unique passwords and enable multi-factor authentication.</li>
        <li>Update operating systems, browsers, and apps consistently.</li>
        <li>Back up important files and verify recovery steps.</li>
        <li>Review attachments before opening them.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Protection works best when simple habits are repeated consistently. Good security usually
        comes from layers: stronger authentication, timely patching, reliable backups, and slower,
        more careful decisions before opening files or links.
      </p>
    </div>
    <img class="hero-image" src="/img/protection-illustration.svg" alt="Cybersecurity protection illustration">
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2>Defense Strategy</h2>
    <p class="section-note">
      Protection is stronger when technical controls and user habits support each other.
    </p>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="data-card">
        <p class="card-label">Authentication</p>
        <h3>Reduce account compromise</h3>
        <p>Unique passwords and MFA make credential theft less useful to attackers.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="data-card">
        <p class="card-label">Updates</p>
        <h3>Close known weaknesses</h3>
        <p>Regular updates reduce exposure to vulnerabilities that attackers already understand.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="data-card">
        <p class="card-label">Backups</p>
        <h3>Recover faster</h3>
        <p>Backups limit damage from ransomware, deletion, and accidental data loss.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="data-card">
        <p class="card-label">Verification</p>
        <h3>Pause before opening files</h3>
        <p>Reviewing links, senders, and attachments helps stop phishing before malware is delivered.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>
